  "description": "Design a shopping cart with coupons (Amazon, Meesho, Swiggy, Flipkart): stock checks, eligibility rules as Specifications, discounts as Strategies stacked in a fixed order, and an all-or-nothing checkout, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 55 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 22 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Shopping Cart, Coupons &amp; Discounts</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Build the cart that Amazon, Meesho, Microsoft, Swiggy and Flipkart keep asking for: add, update and remove items, check stock, apply coupons with rules (minimum cart value, category, first order, expiry, usage limit), stack them in a fixed order, and check out without overselling the last unit. You get the requirements, the class model, three patterns and why each earns its place (Specification, Strategy, Decorator), running Java, Python and C++14 code, a 90-minute plan and the follow-ups interviewers ask.</p>\n"
  },
